== fm-claude-permission
ok - one permission request produces one durable decision signal without answering or changing busy state
ok - a resume event closes the permission decision exactly once
ok - later requests and replacement incarnations remain distinct; stale and malformed events are refused
exit=
== fm-busy-adapter-wiring
ok - pi extension events from a superseded incarnation are rejected as stale
ok - kimi and grok install no unverified semantic wiring and classify through their own gates
ok - opencode 1.x plugin classifies from session.status and ignores OpenCode 2 session.execution.* events
ok - opencode plugin classifies from session.execution.* (OpenCode 2), scoped to the latched worker session
ok - claude hooks open on UserPromptSubmit and close on Stop, StopFailure, and SessionEnd
ok - claude hook events from a superseded incarnation are rejected without breaking the hook
ok - gemini hooks open on BeforeAgent and close on AfterAgent and a repeated SessionEnd
ok - gemini hook events from a superseded incarnation are rejected without breaking the hook
ok - raw gemini launch remains unwired and classifies unknown
ok - gemini is refused as a secondmate because it has no primary supervision protocol
ok - kiro hooks open on userPromptSubmit and close on stop, keeping the turn-end touch
ok - kiro hook events from a superseded incarnation are rejected without breaking the hook
ok - raw kiro launch remains unwired and classifies unknown
ok - codex classifies unknown until a semantic source is verified, never idle or footer-matched
all fm-busy-adapter-wiring tests passed
exit=
== fm-backend-t3code
ok - fm-spawn.sh backend=t3code: compatible tracked Codex config launches, stays out of commits, and survives cleanup
ok - tracked Codex overlay: edited files survive refusal, interrupted restoration recovers, quoted and dotted policy keys refuse
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code codex: refuses to overwrite a project's tracked .codex/config.toml before any mutation
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code claude: refuses to overwrite a project's tracked CLAUDE.local.md before any mutation
ok - Claude channel refuses a symlink in the leased worktree without following it
ok - untracked Codex config is preserved unless Firstmate's marker owns it
ok - fm-t3code-codex-env.sh cleanup: without an installed overlay it needs no Python and never refuses
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code codex: an untracked Codex config in the main checkout does not refuse a worker
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code codex: writes .codex/config.toml with GOTMPDIR, FM_TASK_ID, and TRACEPARENT
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code codex: warns once, and still launches, unless the Codex configuration trusts the launch directory's main checkout
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code --secondmate: project on the home, root-strategy thread, charter message, launch prefix as settings env
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code --secondmate codex: launch prefix as .codex/config.toml shell_environment_policy
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code: refuses before mutation when the credential is rejected
ok - fm-teardown.sh backend=t3code: interrupts and archives the thread with a proven close, then returns the slot
ok - fm-teardown.sh backend=t3code secondmate: interrupts and archives, then ends the home's lingering provider process before the home is removed; an unprovable scan keeps the home
exit=
